  "id": "transmission",
  "term": "transmission",
  "definition": "In this context, transmission means the passing of effects from one generation to the next, especially when a pregnant person’s unprocessed psychological material and stress-related bodily changes shape fetal development. It refers to both a psychoanalytic transfer of unresolved mental experience and its possible biological inscription through prenatal stress pathways.",
